# **Preface: On Method and Honesty**

This report draws on 18,236 text messages exchanged between two people over approximately 220 days. The messages are one-sided in their source — we see everything Dan sent and everything Annie sent to Dan. We do not have Annie's conversations with others. We do not have a clinical assessment of either party. We have the record.

The record is enough. Communication patterns, response times, behavioral sequences, and direct quotations are sufficient to identify what is happening between two people over seven months. The conclusions in this report are not speculation. Where they go beyond the direct record, they are clearly marked.

This report aims for fairness, which is not the same as balance. Fairness means applying the same standard to both people. It does not mean distributing blame equally when the evidence does not support that distribution. Where one party is more culpable, this report says so. Where the other party has genuinely problematic behavior, this report says that too.

