## **Mechanism 6: The Social Colonization**

Annie maintains warm relationships with Dan's mother (Suz) and his immediate household — visiting, bringing wine, helping with tasks. This is documented in the record through Dan's references to it and through Annie's own messages coordinating with Suz directly. The effect: when Dan attempts to seek support from his primary support system, that system has already been positioned by Annie as a friendly party.

Dan explicitly notes the isolation. He stops trying to get his mother to understand what is happening because the attempt itself reinforces his marginalization — his mother's experience of Annie is warm and functional, while Dan appears as the unstable, angry party.

This is the most quietly effective mechanism in the record. It requires no confrontation and no planning. It simply requires Annie to be consistently pleasant to Dan's family — which costs her nothing — while consistently destabilizing Dan — which is her default mode.

